// TerrainTranscode.kdl
//
// Purpose:
// - Loose, user-editable Classic Client -> Enhanced Client terrain slot map.
// - Loaded by the app from `assets/cc_ec_convtables/TerrainTranscode.kdl`.
// - When `tex_land_ec.uddp` is loaded, this loose file can override the
//   embedded transcode map without repacking UDDP files.
//
// Data model:
// - Each `t` node maps one EC terrain/runtime slot id to one or more CC terrain
//   tile ids.
// - Syntax:
//
//     t EC_ID CC_ID...
//
// - `EC_ID`: unsigned integer. Runtime EC land/material slot to use.
// - `CC_ID...`: one or more unsigned integers. Classic land tile ids that
//   should resolve to `EC_ID`.
//
// Example:
//
//     // Water
//     t 5 168 169 170 171
//
//   This means CC land tiles 168, 169, 170, and 171 all use EC runtime slot 5.
//
// Conflict behavior:
// - If the same CC id appears in multiple `t` rows, the later row wins because
//   the loader builds a `HashMap<cc_id, ec_id>` by inserting rows in file order.
// - Avoid intentional duplicates unless the point is to override an earlier
//   broad grouping.
//
// Relationship to other files:
// - `TerrainDefinition.uop` and packed `tex_land_ec.uddp` provenance remain the
//   source-derived material evidence.
// - `TerrainTranscode.kdl` is a practical runtime routing map, mainly for
//   grouping many CC land ids onto one EC terrain slot.
// - `EcTerrainOverrides.kdl` is for reviewed material integration details
//   attached to an EC material/slot, such as policies, liquid motion, or layer
//   texture overrides.
// - `EcSurfaceOverrides.kdl` is for item/static surface-like art routing, not
//   map land tile routing.
//
// Comments:
// - `// line comments` and `/* block comments */` are stripped before parsing
//   by this loader.
// - The category comments below are human labels only; they are not parsed.
//
// Void / No-Draw
t 0 1 2 127 129 132 328 329 331 431 432 433 434 435 436 437 1006 1007 1008 1010 1011 1012 1229 12519

